         main.tex: §4 'Measured largest Lyapunov exponent (EXP-LY-01)' replaced the Discretised proxy;
         §6.3 'Basin volume (Monte-Carlo, EXP-MC-01)'; new §7 'Topological Viability Signature (EXP-TDA-01)'.
         Abstract + §Contributions + §Open-Questions Q4 updated. 3 figures generated and wired:
         fig8_basin_volume (matplotlib), fig9_topology (ripser persistence diagram, n02 tda-venv),
         fig10_lyapunov (running λ_max). Paper compiles clean, 41pp. All figure numbers reproduce the
         results.vsm exactly (λ_max=-0.010050, basin vol 1.0, H0=0.2535/H1=0.0032). Binary dumps added to
         main.rs analysis subcommands (VSF_MC_CSV; dense LY checkpoints). This file is now historical."

trilogy_framing:
  "Three independent rigorous lenses on the SAME convergence/viability thesis, each closing a documented
   review_calibration objection OR adding a novel angle:
     DYNAMICS  — EXP-LY-01: measured λ_max < 0 (Benettin) replaces the 'Discretised proxy' (§Lyapunov).
     VOLUME    — EXP-MC-01: Monte-Carlo basin volume ≈ 1.0 replaces the sparse 6-δ basin sweep.
     SHAPE     — EXP-TDA-01: persistent homology β₀=1∧β₁=0 (point sink) — novel topological signature."

integrations:
  EXP-MC-01_basin_volume:
    where:   "augment §Experiment 'Basin Geometry' (currently multi-kernel) with a 'Basin Volume' subsection;
              or extend §Open Questions Q3/Q7."
    claim:   "basin_volume_fraction = 1.0 (200/200 recover); random-direction floor 0.945; EXP-AB-01's
              0.875 is the WORST-CASE (ground-state corner). Density estimate, not 6 hand-picked δ."
    closes:  "review_calibration objection: 'basin floor from sparse hand-picked deltas'."
    source:  "docs/experiments/EXP-MC-01/{spec,results}.vsm ; binary basin_mc."
  EXP-TDA-01_topology:
    where:   "NEW section 'Topological Viability Signature' (after Basin Geometry)."
    claim:   "VR persistent homology: β₀=1 ∧ β₁=0 (single attractor, no hole) over a wide ε-plateau
              (H_TDA1, ~80× signal/noise); raw-cosine sufficient — no projection (H_TDA2, D_eff≈3);
              perturbation+recovery is CONTRACTIBLE — β₁=0 even at δ=10 kick (H_TDA3) ⇒ topological POINT
              SINK, no limit cycle. β₀=1 holds ON and OFF the attractor."
    closes:  "adds a novel topological angle; reinforces D_eff≈3 (reframes the 'D_KY is a proxy' concern)."
    source:  "docs/experiments/EXP-TDA-01/{seed,prereqs_standup,results}.vsm ; scripts/tda/ ; /home/rmw3/tda-venv."
  EXP-LY-01_lyapunov:   // DONE 2026-06-02
    where:   "§Lyapunov Convergence — REPLACE the 'Discretised proxy' subsection with the measured exponent."
    claim:   "λ_max = -0.01005/tick = ln(0.99) (Benettin, machine precision) < 0 ⇒ rigorous contraction,
              replacing the mean_dL proxy. All-negative ⇒ KY-dim=0 point sink. Clarifies D_eff (active-dim
              heuristic) ≠ KY-dimension."
    closes:  "review_calibration objections: 'Lyapunov is a proof sketch' AND 'D_KY is a proxy'."
    source:  "docs/experiments/lyapunov_spectrum/{spec,results}.vsm ; binary lyapunov_spectrum."
  TRILOGY_COMPLETE: "all three lenses confirmed (LY-01 dynamics + MC-01 volume + TDA-01 shape) — a stable
              point attractor from independent angles. Ready to integrate as a coherent 'rigorous geometry
              of viability' block when the paper is resumed."

figures_needed:    // 'construir gráficos para afirmar la propuesta' — extend plot_results.py
  fig_basin_volume:  "recovery-rate vs κ band (all 1.0) + histogram of stasis_cos_min (worst-case 0.875,
                      typical 0.945). Data: basin_mc telemetry / a CSV dump of the N trials."
  fig_topology:      "β₀(ε) and β₁(ε) curves showing the stable plateau (β₀=1, β₁=0) + a persistence
                      diagram (H0 long bar, H1 at noise). Data: ripser output from tda_calibrate (add a
                      --emit-diagram option to dump births/deaths)."
  fig_lyapunov:      "running λ_max(t) converging to a negative value (Benettin). Data: EXP-LY-01 output."
  note:              "plot_results.py (31KB) is the existing figure generator — add these three. The TDA
                      figs need ripser persistence-diagram data exported (small script addition)."

action_when_resumed:
  "1. write the 3 sections/subsections into main.tex (Basin Volume aug, new Topology section, Lyapunov
      proxy→measured). 2. add the 3 figures to plot_results.py + figures/. 3. update the abstract +
      §Contributions to mention the trilogy. 4. update review_calibration: mark the 2 closed objections."

