pending_2026_06_20:
  status: "INTEGRATED 2026-06-20 + S5 SIGNED OFF 2026-06-21 (rmw3). emergent_thermal_envelope added as
           \\begin{remark}{rem:emergent_envelope} in §sec:thermal_ceiling (Exp 7, where 0.9377 lives, p27):
           0.9377 is an EMERGENT real-system invariant, NOT a basin constant; forward sim bounds synthetic
           excursion ≥0.997 (entropy) / ≥0.999 (thermal); gap structural (scalar channel moves minority of
           128 dims). Framed conservatively (forward-sim, no CH.c machinery named). Model-honesty point."

  emergent_thermal_envelope:  // CHc Alt D finding
    where:   "§6 (or §sec:psi); new subsection 'Emergent Thermal Envelope vs Synthetic Basin Envelope'."
    claim:   "θ_PSI=0.9377 (EXP-CA-01, critical_angle, 18.2°) is NOT an intrinsic basin constant of
              the KernelStepper's Boltzmann attractor — it is an EMERGENT PROPERTY of the full VSF
              system under real hardware thermal load. Evidence (CHc Alt D, 2026-06-20):
              (1) KernelStepper (globally contracting, λ_max=ln(0.99)<0) produces excursion envelopes
              bounded at ~0.997–0.999 for ALL synthetic perturbation classes tested:
                occupation (p→uniform): min_cos_fixed=0.9972
                sustained W4b pressure (p=1.0, 500 ticks, frozen stasis): min_cos_fixed=0.9990
              (2) The gap to 0.9377 is structural, not a model deficiency: the W4b channel moves only
              12 of 128 dims (Block B:8 + Block D:4); the remaining 116 dims (trust ring [0..9],
              Block F stasis embeddings [64..95], Block E signals [48..63]) are unmoved by the scalar
              pressure channel alone. cosine_similarity in ℝ¹²⁸ is dominated by the 116 unmoved dims.
              (3) EXP-CA-01 ran on REAL hardware (actual CPU temperature, real worker-thread contention,
              stasis reference accumulated under sustained load) — the 0.9377 encodes the operational
              stress manifold of the REAL system, not a synthetic basin boundary.
              Implication: the frontier between simulation and real-system behaviour is measurable and
              documentable. The forward model (KernelStepper, CH.c) characterises the synthetic envelope
              correctly; the hardware thermal envelope is a separate real-system invariant requiring live
              measurement (EXP-CA-01 or equivalent). The model does NOT overfit to the measured value —
              it characterises its own domain honestly. [[feedback_validation_loop_no_concessions]]"
    data:    "checo_whatif.rs thermal_dim_analysis: peak_cos=0.9906 (Block B 74%+D 13%+G 8%+A 5%+C 5%).
              sweep_sustained: pressure [0→1] → min_cos_fixed [1.0000→0.9990], span=0.001, gap=+0.0613
              at p=1.0. Source: LXC 108 test run 2026-06-20."
    figure:  "candidate §6 figure: excursion envelope by perturbation class (bar chart):
                occupation perturbation:  min_cos=0.9972
                W4b sustained max:        min_cos=0.9990
                real hardware thermal:    min_cos=0.9377  (EXP-CA-01, measured)
              Three classes, three envelopes — the gap IS the finding."
    gated_on: "Opus paper session (post CHECO 70%); coordinate with §sec:trustlaw/maxwell."

